{%- comment -%}
  Homepage-only presentation tweaks.

  Hides the collection-tab bar under the section heading — the row that reads
  "SUMMER SETS WOMEN" under POPULAR PRODUCTS, and "T-SHIRTS (Men)" under the
  second one.

  Those are not labels, they are the tab buttons of the theme's collection-tabs
  component. Both sections currently carry exactly one tab, so the bar is a
  redundant restatement of what the products already show, and hiding it costs
  no navigation.

  The rule deliberately only matches a bar with a single tab: if a second
  collection is ever added to one of these sections, the tabs become real
  navigation and reappear on their own. Hiding them unconditionally would
  silently strand shoppers on whichever collection happened to be first.

  `visibility: hidden` would leave the row's height behind, so this uses
  `display: none` to close the gap as well.

  Scoped to `.template-index` so collection-tabs sections used on any other
  page are untouched.
{%- endcomment -%}

<style>
  .template-index .section-collection-tabs
    .collection-tabs__list:not(:has(.collection-tabs__list-link + .collection-tabs__list-link)) {
    display: none;
  }
</style>
